My rogue got poisoned by eating a tainted corpse (I ate a corpse of a
creature I had killed without seeing by throwing daggers in a corridor,
it must have been a zombie).
Since I had prayed approximately 300 turns ago, I figured prayer
was not the solution, so I decided to quaff unidentified potions.
1st try: healing (good, but not enough)
2nd try: confusion
3d try: I got the message "You feel a little strange. You feel like a
new woman!"

So it was a potion of polymorph, and it cured me of my poisoning!
I knew polymorphing cured you of hunger, but I had no idea that it
cured other things.
I used to convert all of my polymorph potions into holy water, I
think I might consider them with a new respect after that.

The funny thing is, I think I would never have tried to quaff this
potion had it been identified, at least not before trying to
pray.


